Bright, cheerful cartoon illustration, wide 16:9 format, flat clean colors, bold outlines. Setting: one sunny village riverside square. Absolutely no text, no letters, no numbers, no signs and no labels anywhere. Draw every character and object listed below exactly as described, each only once, and nothing else of importance. Characters from left to right: 1. A fisherman in a bright yellow raincoat and yellow rain hat: he pours blue water from a green teapot into a big red-and-white striped jar; the blue stream visibly goes into the jar; on his back he carries a wicker basket holding exactly three fish. 2. A bald baker in a red apron: he presses a yellow sticky note onto the front cover of a big purple book that he holds against his chest; beside him stands a tray with exactly two loaves of bread. 3. An old man with a long white beard in a green robe: he turns a golden key in the lock of a small black box on his knees, and a tiny glowing star rises out of the opened box; next to him burn exactly three white candles. 4. A knight in shiny silver armor without a helmet plume: he pulls a round golden hand mirror up out of the ground with clumps of soil falling from it, holding it toward a small brown dog; exactly two shovels stand stuck in the ground behind him. No text, no letters, no numbers.